.TH BILTERM 1 "2026-10-25" "bilterm 1.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bilterm \- IBM 3270 Mainframe & DOS Borland Turbo Vision inspired TUI multiplexer, composite-pane shell wrapper, remote SSH fleet manager, and AI-automatable terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bilterm
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbilterm\fR is a terminal user interface (TUI) multiplexer, shell wrapper, and terminal emulator written in Rust + Ratatui. Each terminal pane is a \fBComposite Window Pane\fR pairing a movable, resizable \fBFloatingCommandPrompt\fR (\fB==> \fR) and an \fBIBM 3270 Operator Information Area (OIA)\fR status bar over a full-height scrolling PTY \fBOutputCanvas\fR with zero \fBSIGWINCH\fR geometry thrashing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-mcp\fR
Run the Model Context Protocol (MCP \fB2024-11-05\fR) JSON-RPC 2.0 server over standard input/output for AI agents.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-headless\fR, \fB\-\-daemon\fR [\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-listen\fR \fIIP:PORT|localhost:PORT|unix:PATH\fR]
Run a headless Bilterm workspace daemon serving the JSON-RPC 2.0 automation control plane. Default endpoint is a private Unix domain socket ($XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bilterm/bilterm.sock or /tmp/bilterm-<uid>/bilterm.sock, mode 0600). TCP listeners are restricted to loopback addresses unless \fB\-r\fR / \fB\-\-allow\-remote\fR is specified.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-listen\fR \fIADDR\fR
Listen address (\fIIP:PORT\fR, \fIlocalhost:PORT\fR, or \fIunix:PATH\fR).
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-allow\-remote\fR
Allow binding the JSON-RPC daemon to non-loopback TCP addresses. Requires \fB\-t\fR / \fB\-\-token\-file\fR.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR
Path to a private file (mode 0600) containing the bearer authentication token for the JSON-RPC control plane. Can also be set via the \fBBILTERM_TOKEN_FILE\fR environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-snapshot\-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR
Directory for confined workspace snapshots (defaults to $XDG_STATE_HOME/bilterm/snapshots). Direct RPC and MCP snapshot requests must specify a single file name within this directory.
.TP
\fBctl\fR [\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fIENDPOINT\fR] \fIMETHOD\fR [\fIPARAMS_JSON\fR]
Send a JSON-RPC 2.0 request to a running Bilterm instance and print the JSON result. Default endpoint is the local private Unix domain socket.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-playbook\fR \fIPATH.toml\fR
Execute a declarative TOML automation playbook against an embedded workspace and exit.
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-gui\-dump\fR \fIPATH.ppm\fR
Render the workspace via \fBGuiWorkspaceRenderer\fR to a Netpbm P6 \fB.ppm\fR pixel framebuffer.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fINAME\fR
Use named persistent command-history session (overrides \fBhistory_session\fR).
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH.toml\fR
Load configuration from custom TOML file path.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-completions\fR \fIbash|zsh|fish\fR
Print shell completion script for the specified shell to standard output.
.TP
\fB\-M\fR, \fB\-\-man\fR
Print this roff manual page to standard output.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help summary.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
\fBF1\fR / \fB:help\fR
Toggle interactive Borland Turbo Vision Help Modal.
.TP
\fBCtrl+P\fR / \fBAlt+Space\fR / \fB:palette\fR
Open interactive Fuzzy Command Palette (\fBnucleo-matcher\fR).
.TP
\fBF2\fR (\fBAlt+H\fR) / \fBAlt+V\fR
Split focused composite pane horizontally or vertically.
.TP
\fBF5\fR / \fBAlt+Z\fR
Toggle zoom/maximize on focused composite pane.
.TP
\fBF6\fR (\fBAlt+Tab\fR) / \fBAlt+1..9\fR
Shuffle Z-order window deck or selectively raise pane #1..#9.
.TP
\fBF7\fR (\fBAlt+Shift+D\fR) / \fB:drawer\fR
Toggle \fBherdr\fR-style Slide-Out Sessions/Windows/Panes & Fleet Drawer (supports \fBLeft\fR/\fBRight\fR/\fBTop\fR/\fBBottom\fR docking, \fBOnDemand\fR/\fBFixed\fR/\fBAutoHide\fR, and \fBOverlay\fR/\fBPush\fR modes).
.TP
\fBCtrl++\fR / \fBCtrl+\-\fR / \fBCtrl+0\fR / \fB:fontsize\fR
Dynamically scale terminal text and font size (\fB50%..=300%\fR) across GUI SVG/PPM and TUI DEC \fBDECDWL\fR/\fBDECDHL\fR views.
.TP
\fB:canvas\fR / \fB:tek\fR
Drive Tektronix 4010/4014 vector storage-tube emulation and the modern retained scene-graph (2D sprites, live plots, interactive image inspector) rendered via Unicode Braille/Sextant/Quadrant sub-cells.
.TP
\fBF9\fR / \fB:inspector\fR
Toggle Live 3270 Terminal Inspector modal.
.TP
\fBF10\fR / \fBAlt+\`\fR / \fB:quake\fR
Toggle persistent Guake/Quake drop-down quick terminal.
.TP
\fBF12\fR / \fBCtrl+G\fR / \fB:raw\fR
Toggle between \fBINPUT: CMD BOX\fR and \fBINPUT: RAW PTY\fR.
.TP
\fBAlt+F\fR / \fB:hints\fR
Activate QuickSelect 3270 Field Hints (\fB[a]..[z]\fR) for URLs, paths, IPv4s, and Git SHAs.
.TP
\fBAlt+C\fR / \fB:copy\fR
Enter keyboard-driven Vi Copy Mode & rectangular block selection.
.TP
\fBAlt+L\fR / \fB:lock\fR
Toggle Read-Only Protected 3270 Field Lock (\fBPROT\fR).
.TP
\fBCtrl+Q\fR / \fB:quit\fR
Cleanly exit Bilterm.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/bilterm/config.toml\fR
Declarative user configuration file (themes, outlines, shadows, keybindings, triggers).
.TP
\fI~/.local/state/bilterm/history/\fR
Per-session, per-pane timestamped command history logs.
.TP
\fI~/.local/state/bilterm/sessions/\fR
Saved multi-pane workspace session snapshots (\fB:session save|restore|list\fR).
.SH SECURITY
Bilterm enforces defense-in-depth across automation and shell integration surfaces:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBHeadless Daemon Defaults\fR: Serves on a private 0600 Unix domain socket by default, restricting access to the owning user and verifying peer credentials on every connection.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNetwork Listen Policy\fR: Non-loopback TCP listeners strictly require \fB\-\-allow\-remote\fR and a bearer token loaded from a mode 0600 file. The bearer token is validated via an initial \fBauth.login\fR handshake before any request is processed. Note that \fB\-\-allow\-remote\fR transmits the bearer token in plaintext; an SSH tunnel or VPN is strongly recommended when accessing Bilterm over untrusted networks.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFilesystem Confinement\fR: Direct RPC and MCP workspace snapshots are strictly confined to a single file name within the snapshot directory ($XDG_STATE_HOME/bilterm/snapshots), rejecting directory traversal and refusing to follow planted symlinks. Bilterm-managed temporary files (shell integration rc scripts, command history exports, asciicast recordings, and SSH control paths) reside in per-user private 0700 runtime directories with exclusive 0600 file creation.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSSH Destination Validation\fR: Remote SSH destinations reject options beginning with '\-' to prevent argument injection, and arguments are separated with '\-\-' before destinations.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBBILTERM_TOKEN_FILE\fR
Path to a private 0600 file containing the bearer token for JSON-RPC authentication.
.TP
\fBXDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR
Directory used for Bilterm's private runtime files and default Unix domain socket.
.TP
\fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR
Base directory for Bilterm state files, history logs, and snapshot outputs.
